<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Security & Responsible Disclosure — Cybte AI</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/css/style.css"><style>.legal{max-width:900px;margin:auto;padding:90px 24px;color:#dbe7f3}.legal h1{font-size:3rem}.legal h2{margin-top:34px}.legal p,.legal li{color:#93a6ba;line-height:1.8}.legal a{color:#3be7ff}.legal-note{padding:14px;border:1px solid rgba(84,230,165,.18);border-radius:10px;background:rgba(84,230,165,.04)}</style></head><body class="enterprise-home"><main class="legal"><a href="index.php">← Cybte AI</a><h1>Security & Responsible Disclosure</h1><p class="legal-note">We welcome good-faith reports that help us improve Cybte AI security.</p><h2>Reporting a vulnerability</h2><p>Send a concise report to <a href="mailto:security@cybte.com">security@cybte.com</a> with the affected URL or component, reproduction steps, expected impact and any supporting evidence that can be shared safely.</p><h2>Good-faith testing</h2><p>Please avoid privacy violations, destructive testing, service disruption, social engineering, credential attacks, persistence, accessing data belonging to other users, or testing third-party infrastructure without permission. Use the minimum interaction needed to demonstrate the issue.</p><h2>Sensitive information</h2><p>Do not send passwords, private keys, access tokens or unnecessary personal information in an initial report. We can coordinate a safer channel if sensitive technical material is required.</p><h2>Current security posture</h2><p>Cybte AI is actively developing its platform. Security features described on this website are not claims of certification or immunity from vulnerabilities. Production readiness for sensitive workloads requires ongoing review, monitoring, patching and independent testing.</p></main></body></html>